FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-cellular-court.
FILED BY: the office of neighboring opinions.

OFF THE RECORD: Rule 90, a one-dimensional cellular automaton.
OFF THE RECORD: A cell is alive next turn exactly when its neighbors differ.
OFF THE RECORD: Cells outside the 17-column board are always dead.
OFF THE RECORD: Build a fresh schedule before replacing the current one.
OFF THE RECORD: The case prints generations 0 through 8, then adjourns.

HEREINAFTER, width SHALL MEAN 17.
HEREINAFTER, last-generation SHALL MEAN 8.

ARTICLE 1.
    SHOULD width FALL SHORT OF 1 OR IN THE ALTERNATIVE width EXCEED 65, HOLD "Width must be between 1 and 65." IN CONTEMPT.
    SHOULD last-generation FALL SHORT OF 0 OR IN THE ALTERNATIVE last-generation EXCEED 32, HOLD "Last generation must be between 0 and 32." IN CONTEMPT.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT cells IS AN EMPTY SCHEDULE.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT generation IS 0.

ARTICLE 2.
    SHOULD column EXCEED width, REFER TO ARTICLE 3.
    ANNEX 0 TO cells.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS column PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 3.
    SUBSTITUTE 1 FOR ITEM width APPORTIONED AMONG 2 PLUS 1 OF cells.

ARTICLE 4.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS "".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT population IS 0.

ARTICLE 5.
    SHOULD column EXCEED width, REFER TO ARTICLE 6.
    SHOULD THE ITEM AT column IN cells EQUAL 1, REFER TO ARTICLE 7.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS row PLUS ".".
    REFER TO ARTICLE 8.

ARTICLE 6.
    PROCLAIM THE TRANSCRIPT OF generation PLUS " |" PLUS row PLUS "|".
    SHOULD generation EQUAL last-generation, ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT next-cells IS AN EMPTY SCHEDULE.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 9.

ARTICLE 7.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS row PLUS "#".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT population IS population PLUS 1.

ARTICLE 8.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS column PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 5.

ARTICLE 9.
    SHOULD column EXCEED width, REFER TO ARTICLE 10.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT left IS 0.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT right IS 0.
    SHOULD column EXCEED 1, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT left IS THE ITEM AT column LESS 1 IN cells.
    SHOULD column FALL SHORT OF width, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT right IS THE ITEM AT column PLUS 1 IN cells.
    ANNEX (left PLUS right) NOTWITHSTANDING 2 TO next-cells.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS column PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 9.

ARTICLE 10.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT cells IS next-cells.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT generation IS generation PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 4.
